IMPORT prelude

-- Financial Services and Markets Act 2022 (Singapore) -- prohibition orders and their effect on financial institutions (ss 7, 8),
-- and the licensing regime for digital token service providers in Part 9: who needs a licence (s 137), the conditions of grant
-- (s 138(3)), holding out (s 139), lapse (s 141(1)), the ban on lending to individuals (s 147), controller thresholds and approval
-- (ss 136(1), 149, 153), appeals (ss 7(5), 154) and the general penalty (s 163).
--
-- Edition: Act 18 of 2022 (not a 2020 Revised Edition Act), current version as at 1 October 2026, informal consolidation, as deposited
-- at ../../registers/source-bundle/FSMA2022.txt, with amendments to Act 5 of 2025 (wef 9 March 2025) annotated; one provision of the
-- Act itself is annotated wef 30 June 2025.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 20 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the two places an ordinary person or
-- business meets it directly: being barred from the industry by a prohibition order, and running a digital token business out of
-- Singapore. Not encoded: MAS directions and approvals (Part 2), AML/CFT and foreign assistance (Part 4), the information sharing
-- scheme (Part 4A), technology risk (Part 5), dispute resolution schemes beyond s 36 (Part 6), control and resolution of failing
-- institutions, bail-in and the resolution fund (Parts 7 and 8), inspection and investigation (Parts 10, 10A), the amendments to
-- other Acts (Part 13) and transitional provisions. The First Schedule (what a "digital token service" is) and the Second Schedule
-- (exempt providers) were not read; they are taken as inputs.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Financial Services and Markets Act 2022 -- shared nouns`

DECLARE Person IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a partnership`
    `a Singapore corporation`
    `a foreign corporation`

-- s 137(7): "Singapore corporation" means a body corporate formed or incorporated in Singapore and includes a limited liability
-- partnership.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an individual` IF
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `an individual` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` MEANS IF `a` GREATER THAN `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§ `Part 3 -- prohibition orders`

§§ `7 -- who may be prohibited, and the 5% substantial shareholder`

-- s 7(1): MAS may make a prohibition order "if the Authority is satisfied that the person is not a fit and proper person in
-- accordance with the Guidelines on Fit and Proper Criteria". (4): "must not make a prohibition order against a person without
-- giving the person an opportunity to be heard". (2): permanently or for a specified period.
GIVEN `found not fit and proper` IS A BOOLEAN, `given an opportunity to be heard` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `MAS may make a prohibition order` IF
    `found not fit and proper` AND `given an opportunity to be heard`

-- s 7(7): a substantial shareholder has voting shares (excluding treasury shares) carrying "not less than 5% of the total votes".
-- (8): where there are 2 or more classes, 5% of the votes in "one of those classes" is enough.
GIVEN `percent of votes in the whole company` IS A NUMBER, `largest percent of votes in any one class` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a substantial shareholder` IF
        `percent of votes in the whole company` AT LEAST 5
    OR  `largest percent of votes in any one class` AT LEAST 5

-- s 7(5): appeal to the Minister "within 30 days after the decision".
GIVEN `days since the decision` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an appeal against a prohibition order is in time` IF
    `days since the decision` AT MOST 30

§§ `8 -- effect of a prohibition order`

-- s 8(2): "a financial institution must not employ or enter into any arrangement with A, or use A's service, whether directly or
-- indirectly" to the extent prohibited. (4): fine up to $100,000. (5): a defence of all reasonable steps and reasonable belief is
-- available ONLY where the institution is charged for INDIRECT employment, arrangement or use.
GIVEN `uses a prohibited person within the prohibition` IS A BOOLEAN, `the use is indirect` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `took all reasonable steps and reasonably believed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the financial institution commits an offence under s 8(4)` IF
        `uses a prohibited person within the prohibition`
    AND (NOT (`the use is indirect` AND `took all reasonable steps and reasonably believed otherwise`))

-- s 8(3): the prohibited person who breaches the order -- $150,000 or 2 years or both. s 8(4): the financial institution --
-- $100,000. s 8(8): failing to tell representatives and appointees (6), or a representative who carries on (7) -- $150,000 and
-- $15,000 a day.
DECLARE Breach IS ONE OF
    `the prohibited person breaching the order`
    `an institution using a prohibited person`
    `failing to notify representatives or a representative carrying on`

GIVEN `the breach` IS A Breach
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 8 maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the breach`
    WHEN `the prohibited person breaching the order` THEN 150000
    WHEN `an institution using a prohibited person` THEN 100000
    WHEN `failing to notify representatives or a representative carrying on` THEN 150000

GIVEN `the breach` IS A Breach
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 8 maximum imprisonment in years` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the breach`
    WHEN `the prohibited person breaching the order` THEN 2
    OTHERWISE 0

-- s 8(9): a prohibition order does not "avoid or affect any agreement, transaction or arrangement entered into by the person against
-- whom the order is made". Encoded as: the order never voids the person's contracts.
GIVEN `entered into before the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the prohibition order voids the contract` IF
    FALSE

§ `Part 9 -- digital token service providers`

§§ `137 -- who needs a licence`

-- s 137(1): "an individual or a partnership must not from a place of business in Singapore carry on a business of providing any
-- type of digital token service outside Singapore unless" licensed. (3): "a Singapore corporation must not carry on a business,
-- whether from Singapore or elsewhere, of providing any type of digital token service outside Singapore" unless licensed.
-- (2), (4): a person providing the service while carrying on any other business is presumed to carry on a business of providing it,
-- and the presumption "is not rebutted by proof that the provision ... is related or incidental" to the primary business.
-- (5): no licence is needed where the provider is licensed or exempt under the Securities and Futures Act 2001, Financial Advisers
-- Act 2001 or Payment Services Act 2019 for that activity, is in the Second Schedule, or is in a prescribed class.
--
-- The regime bites on services provided OUTSIDE Singapore. A foreign corporation is named in neither (1) nor (3): INFERENCE, it is
-- outside s 137 entirely.
GIVEN `the provider` IS A Person, `operates from a place of business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `provides the service outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `the service is only incidental to another business` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `excluded by s 137(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a digital token licence is required` IF
        `provides the service outside Singapore`
    AND (NOT `excluded by s 137(5)`)
    AND (CONSIDER `the provider`
         WHEN `an individual` THEN `operates from a place of business in Singapore`
         WHEN `a partnership` THEN `operates from a place of business in Singapore`
         WHEN `a Singapore corporation` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a foreign corporation` THEN FALSE)

-- s 137(6) and s 139(5): individual -- $125,000 or 3 years or both, plus $12,500 a day; "any other case" -- $250,000, plus $25,000
-- a day. s 153(2) uses the same scale for controller offences.
GIVEN `the offender` IS A Person
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Part 9 maximum fine` MEANS
    IF `is an individual` `the offender` THEN 125000 ELSE 250000

GIVEN `the offender` IS A Person
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Part 9 maximum daily fine` MEANS
    IF `is an individual` `the offender` THEN 12500 ELSE 25000

GIVEN `the offender` IS A Person
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Part 9 maximum imprisonment in years` MEANS
    IF `is an individual` `the offender` THEN 3 ELSE 0

-- s 163: for an offence under Part 9 "for which no penalty is expressly provided": individual $50,000; any other case $100,000.
GIVEN `the offender` IS A Person
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Part 9 general penalty` MEANS
    IF `is an individual` `the offender` THEN 50000 ELSE 100000

§§ `138(3) -- conditions for grant`

-- s 138(3): MAS "must not grant the licence" unless (a) a permanent place of business in Singapore; (b)-(d) an executive director,
-- partner or LLP partner/manager resident in Singapore (or of a prescribed class); (e) prescribed financial requirements; (f) MAS is
-- satisfied as to fitness and propriety, financial condition, public interest and other criteria; (g) operational requirements;
-- (h) information and a non-refundable fee. (2): even then MAS "may" grant or refuse. (5): no refusal without a hearing.
GIVEN `has a permanent place of business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `has a resident executive director or partner` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `meets financial and operational requirements` IS A BOOLEAN, `MAS is satisfied on fitness, finances and public interest` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `paid the fee and supplied the documents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `MAS is permitted to grant the licence` IF
        `has a permanent place of business in Singapore`
    AND `has a resident executive director or partner`
    AND `meets financial and operational requirements`
    AND `MAS is satisfied on fitness, finances and public interest`
    AND `paid the fee and supplied the documents`

§§ `139 -- holding out`

-- s 139(1): "A person must not hold himself, herself or itself out as a licensee, unless the person has in force a licence."
-- (2), (3): nor hold out as carrying on the business outside Singapore unless a licensee or exempt under s 189; (4): (2) and (3) do
-- not apply to a person mentioned in s 137(5). The s 137(5) carve-out does not reach (1).
GIVEN `claims to be a licensee` IS A BOOLEAN, `claims to provide the service outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `holds a licence` IS A BOOLEAN, `exempt under s 189` IS A BOOLEAN, `excluded by s 137(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the holding out is an offence` IF
        (`claims to be a licensee` AND (NOT `holds a licence`))
    OR  (    `claims to provide the service outside Singapore`
         AND (NOT `holds a licence`)
         AND (NOT `exempt under s 189`)
         AND (NOT `excluded by s 137(5)`))

§§ `141(1) -- lapse`

-- s 141(1): a licence lapses (a) for an entity, if it "is wound up or otherwise dissolved, whether in Singapore or elsewhere";
-- (b) for an individual, if the licensee "dies, becomes mentally incapacitated or is adjudicated a bankrupt"; (c) on a prescribed event.
DECLARE Event IS ONE OF
    `the licensee is wound up or dissolved`
    `the individual licensee dies`
    `the individual licensee becomes mentally incapacitated`
    `the individual licensee is made bankrupt`
    `the licensee makes a loss`
    `the licensee changes its name`

GIVEN `the event` IS A Event
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licence lapses automatically` IF
    CONSIDER `the event`
    WHEN `the licensee makes a loss` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the licensee changes its name` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `147 -- no lending to individuals`

-- s 147(1): "A licensee must not carry on a business of granting any credit facility to any individual in Singapore." (2): $100,000,
-- plus $10,000 a day. (3): a credit facility is an advance, loan or other facility to an individual customer, or a liability
-- incurred on an individual customer's behalf. Lending to a corporate customer, or to an individual outside Singapore, is not caught.
GIVEN `the borrower is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `the borrower is in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licensee may not grant the credit` IF
    `the borrower is an individual` AND `the borrower is in Singapore`

§§ `136(1), 149 and 153 -- controllers`

-- s 136(1): a 5% controller has, alone or with associates, at least 5% but less than 12% of the shares or votes; a 12% controller
-- at least 12% but less than 20%; a 20% controller at least 20%. Either limb suffices, so the larger figure decides the band.
DECLARE Band IS ONE OF
    `not a controller`
    `a 5% controller`
    `a 12% controller`
    `a 20% controller`

GIVEN `stake` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Band
`the band for a stake` MEANS
    IF `stake` AT LEAST 20 THEN `a 20% controller`
    ELSE (IF `stake` AT LEAST 12 THEN `a 12% controller` ELSE (IF `stake` AT LEAST 5 THEN `a 5% controller` ELSE `not a controller`))

GIVEN `percent of shares` IS A NUMBER, `percent of votes` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Band
`the controller band` MEANS
    `the band for a stake` (`the larger of` `percent of shares` `percent of votes`)

-- s 149(1): "A person must not become a 20% controller of a licensee without first applying for and obtaining the approval of the
-- Authority". Only the 20% band needs approval; the 5% and 12% bands matter for revocation (s 141(2)(a)(v)).
GIVEN `percent of shares` IS A NUMBER, `percent of votes` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `MAS approval is needed first` IF
    `the controller band` `percent of shares` `percent of votes` EQUALS `a 20% controller`

-- s 153(3): defence if the person (a) was not aware of the contravention, (b) notified MAS "within 14 days after becoming aware",
-- and (c) took the action MAS directed. (4): even if aware, a defence where the crossing came from an increase by a family associate
-- (s 136(2)(c)(i)) with no agreement to act together, MAS notified within 14 days after the contravention, and directed action taken.
-- (5): otherwise lack of intent or knowledge is no defence.
GIVEN `was aware of crossing 20%` IS A BOOLEAN, `crossing caused by a family associate with no arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `days until MAS notified` IS A NUMBER, `took the action MAS directed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the controller has a defence` IF
        `days until MAS notified` AT MOST 14
    AND `took the action MAS directed`
    AND ((NOT `was aware of crossing 20%`) OR `crossing caused by a family associate with no arrangement`)

-- s 154: appeal to the Minister "within 30 days after receiving the decision", "whose decision is final".
GIVEN `days since receiving the decision` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a controller appeal is in time` IF
    `days since receiving the decision` AT MOST 30
